hyperactive-interaction-in-the-words-of-the-human-superorganism-6 = unlines (cons (quoted (cons "What intelligence (*intelligere*, to gather between) gathers is data, and *data* is the plural of *datum*, " (cons "given" (cons ". Data is what is given. *Information* is *in-formare*, to give shape to something, to put form into it. So the erasure of meaning around 1970, when storage became untyped bytes, has an exact description in the words: it kept the given and threw away the form. Data without meaning is the given without its shape, and every industry that reconstructs meaning is putting the form back." nil)))) nil)
